    ['Legal hermeneutics distinguishes originalist intent from living constitutionalism in civil rights jurisprudence.', 'Judicial debates over whether antique laws should be interpreted literally or adaptively.', 'School', 'Jurisprudence', 'The theory or philosophy of law', 'Originalist', 'Characterized by viewing constitutional provisions as retaining original meaning'],
